f roadside injuries and deaths than police and other first\nresponders to accident scenes. For one thing, there are usually\npersons on hand to control traffic while others minister to the\ninjured and clear accident scenes. Tow truck and roadside service\ndrivers, on the other hand, are often acting alone.\n\nThe color of flashing lights is another factor. Law enforcement\nofficers are quick to acknowledge that motorists simply don't respect\nyellow lights. More importantly, scientific studies have demonstrated\nthat blue lights are far more visible than any other color.\nHopefully, this bill will provide tow truck and roadside service\ndrivers with greater protection while performing hazardous work\nalongside our state's highways.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew legislation\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
